      "id": 494008,
      "username": "marc_centura",
      "name": " Marc Ramser",
      "created_at": "2026-02-11T13:21:39.802Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Unfurtunatly, I dont know an answer to the orignal problem but I want to warn about the solution proposed here:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><code>sudo</code> makes it run as root, so it affects all files even if the user normally doesn’t have permission.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>chmod -R</code> applies changes <strong>recursively</strong> to the folder and everything inside.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>o+rx</code> gives <strong>read and execute permissions to “others”</strong> (anyone on the system who isn’t the owner or in your group).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>/home/${USER}</code> targets the user’s entire home directory.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So effectively, this command <strong>lets any user on the system read and enter every file and folder in your home directory</strong>.</p>\n<p>Please only do that if you know exaclty what you are doing.</p>",
